        "form": "rad-distribute__numeric"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "c2",
      "kind": "concept",
      "body": "Distribute, then simplify each product — often to a whole number. √3 · (√3 + √12) = √9 + √36 = 3 + 6 = 9. Each piece can collapse to an integer when the radicands multiply to a perfect square.",
      "figure": "rad-distribute"
    },
    {
      "id": "i2",
      "kind": "interactive",
      "body": "Two rope segments.",
      "widget": {
        "type": "numeric",
        "prompt": "Two rope segments measure √20 meters and √5 meters. What is the product of their lengths?",
        "answer": 10,
        "tolerance": 0,
        "commonErrors": [
          {
            "value": 25,
            "feedback": "Multiply the radicands, don't add: √(20 · 5) = √100 = 10."
          },
          {
            "value": 100,
            "feedback": "√100 isn't 100 — take the root: √100 = 10."
          }
        ],
        "fallbackFeedback": "√20 · √5 = √100 = 10."
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "c3",
      "kind": "concept",
      "body": "After distributing, **combine like radicals** if any match. √2 · (√6 + √2) = √12 + √4 = 2√3 + 2. Simplify each product, then merge anything with the same radicand.",
      "figure": "rad-combine-after"
    },
    {
      "id": "i3",
      "kind": "interactive",
      "body": "Multiply, then simplify.",
      "widget": {
        "type": "numeric",
        "prompt": "√2 · √6 = a√3 after simplifying. What is a?",
        "answer": 2,
        "tolerance": 0,
        "commonErrors": [
          {
            "value": 12,
            "feedback": "√2 · √6 = √12, and √12 = 2√3, so a = 2 (not 12)."
          },
          {
            "value": 3,
            "feedback": "3 is the radicand left over. The coefficient from √12 = 2√3 is 2."
          }
        ],
        "fallbackFeedback": "√2 · √6 = √12 = 2√3, so a = 2."
      }
    },
